  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ger">Ger</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-b">[5] Swa sceal god scyrman his hlafordes healdan, do ymbe his agen, swa swa he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="22.7" corresp="#wit-b">Swa sceal god scyrman his hlafor||des Healdan do ymbe his agen swa swa he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b">Swa sceal god scyrman his hlafordes healdan, do ymbe his agen, swa swa he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">Thus a good shireman should maintain his lord’s estate just as he would want concerning his own.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b">A good shire reeve must oversee his lord’s property thus, no matter what he does about his own.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">So soll ein guter Amtmann [das Gut] seines Herrn hüten, mag er betreffend sein eigen handeln, wie er will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">So shall a good reeve guard his lord's [estate], whatever he may do about his own as he wishes.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">‘mag er … handeln’: concessive, after Pogatscher. Liebermann compares Gerefa 12.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
